course: dictionary
lesson: 1499
title: Short forms and what they stand for
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An abbreviation is a short form of a word or phrase. Context tells you which full words it stands for. «A small hole about 13 centimetres wide, roughly the size of a CD, at the bottom of a fence lets hedgehogs travel between gardens.» A hole the size of a disc is not a music player, so CD here means the shiny round disc.
explain: One short form can stand for several things, so look at the words around it. «cd» can be a command in a computer window, and it can be a symbol in science. Ask yourself: what would fit here, and does my meaning still make sense in the sentence?
explain: The hedgehog sentences also show why size matters. «Hedgehogs travel through many gardens to find food and mates, so neighbours cut holes about the size of a CD in their fences to make hedgehog highways.» Read the whole sentence before you decide what the clue means.
fact: An abbreviation is a shortened form of a word, such as CD for compact disc.
fact: A CD is a thin, shiny, round plastic disc that stores music or computer data, read by a laser.
fact: In a computer terminal, «cd» is a command meaning change directory: it moves you to another folder.
fact: In science, «cd» is the symbol for the candela, the unit of light brightness.
fact: Other meanings in context: CD can mean certificate of deposit (money) or corps diplomatique (a diplomat's car sign).
exercise: «A small hole about 13 centimetres wide, roughly the size of a CD, lets hedgehogs travel between gardens.» What is a CD in this sentence? | A folder on a computer | *A thin, shiny, round plastic disc | A small hole in a fence | A type of hedgehog
exercise: In a computer window, you type «cd Pictures» to go into a folder. What does cd mean here? | Compact disc | Candela | Certificate of deposit | *Change directory
exercise: Ella reads «cd» in a science book about light brightness. What does it stand for? | Corps diplomatique | Compact disc | *Candela | Change directory
test: «Neighbours cut holes about the size of a CD in their fences.» What do the holes help to make? | A music player for the garden | A computer folder | *Hedgehog highways | A diplomat's car sign
test: «The bank paid him interest on his CD.» Which meaning fits best? | *Certificate of deposit | Candela | Change directory | Compact disc
exam: Why can the same short form mean different things? | It is a mistake, so it has no meaning at all | All short forms mean exactly the same thing | The computer changes the spelling each time | *The context, meaning the words and setting around it, shows which full words are meant
